From: Holodor <noreply@holodor.local>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: core: dynamically disable timestamp on unsupported devices

When a UFS 4.0+ device rejects `QUERY_ATTR_IDN_TIMESTAMP` with `-EINVAL`,
set `UFS_DEVICE_QUIRK_NO_TIMESTAMP_SUPPORT` so `ufshcd_set_timestamp_attr()`
does not repeatedly fail and log errors on every system resume and RTC
update work tick.
---
 drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -9234,9 +9234,12 @@ static void ufshcd_set_timestamp_attr(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 
 	err = ufshcd_exec_dev_cmd(hba, DEV_CMD_TYPE_QUERY, dev_cmd_timeout);
 
-	if (err)
+	if (err) {
 		dev_err(hba->dev, "%s: failed to set timestamp %d\n",
 			__func__, err);
+		if (err == -EINVAL)
+			hba->dev_quirks |= UFS_DEVICE_QUIRK_NO_TIMESTAMP_SUPPORT;
+	}
 
 	ufshcd_dev_man_unlock(hba);
 }
